  "market_context": "Price had been making lower highs and lower lows (downtrend), then formed a higher high, signaling a break of structure and shift to bullish bias.",
  "key_observation": "After the break of structure (higher high), price retraced precisely to the 0.5 Fibonacci level before resuming upward momentum and extending to the -0.5 and -1 Fibonacci extension targets.",
  "analysis_steps": [
    "Step 1: Identified prior market structure as lower highs and lower lows, confirming a downtrend.",
    "Step 2: Recognized the break of structure when price made a higher high, signaling potential bullish reversal.",
    "Step 3: Drew Fibonacci retracement from the impulse move that broke the structure (swing low to swing high).",
    "Step 4: Observed price retracing to the 0.5 Fibonacci level, which served as the entry/reversal zone.",
    "Step 5: Noted price then extended upward to the -0.5 Fibonacci extension (first profit target) and continued to the full -1 extension."
  ],
  "outcome": null,
  "lessons": "When market structure shifts (e.g., higher high after lower highs), Fibonacci drawn on the impulse move provides high-probability retracement zones (0.5) and extension targets (-0.5, -1) for trend continuation entries.",
